# tests/app.script - the app installed, played and updated as a user would (make test-app;
# --mode none: time 0 = the Desktop is up, Files open at the card's root):
#  1. DIGGER.HZA found in Files by typing its name and opened: the Installer asks (shot 1);
#     Install; its message (shot 2);
#  2. the Programs menu (F10, Right): "Games >" last, End to it, Enter opens its pop-up at
#     the pointer (shot 3), Down, Enter: Digger starts; its title (shot 4);
#  3. a game: up the middle column (125 points), three lives lost, the initials APP: the
#     high score file is written in the app's folder; Esc: back to the Desktop;
#  4. DIGGER.HZA opened again: the Installer offers Replace (shot 5): the update, which
#     must keep DIGGER.SCO (tests/app.sh checks the card).
# (on the board's card, run816's default: the install takes a few seconds, the Desktop then
# reads the new Programs list, and the Programs and Games menus check their programs on the
# card as they open: about 2 s each)
1000 digger\n
+0 wait install: asks
+800 shot
+500 \n
+0 wait install: installed
+800 shot
+500 \n
+6000 {f10}
+400 {right}
+3000 {end}
+400 \n
+3000 shot
+400 {down}
+300 \n
+0 wait digger: title
+1500 shot
+500 key enter 100
+0 wait digger: play
+500 key up 4500
+0 wait digger: dead
+0 wait digger: play
+0 wait digger: dead
+0 wait digger: play
+0 wait digger: dead
+0 wait digger: initials
+500 APP
+0 wait digger: title
+1500 key esc 100
+3000 digger\n
+0 wait install: asks
+800 shot
+500 \n
+0 wait install: replaced
+800 \n
